# Conventional Commits

All commit messages must follow the [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) specification.

## Format

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- **type**: what kind of change (required)
- **scope**: affected package or area, e.g. `ui`, `api`, `db` (optional)
- **description**: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period (required)
- **body**: explain motivation and contrast with previous behavior (optional)
- **footer**: breaking changes, issue refs, e.g. `BREAKING CHANGE:`, `Closes #123` (optional)

## Common Types

| Type | Use when |
|------|----------|
| `feat` | New feature or user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, whitespace; no logic change |
| `refactor` | Code change that is neither feat nor fix |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |
| `chore` | Build, CI, deps, tooling |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |

## Examples

```
feat(ui): add character search page
fix(api): handle null guild id in roster query
docs: update local setup instructions
chore(deps): bump vite to 6.0
refactor(db): extract migration helpers

fix(auth)!: require email verification on signup

BREAKING CHANGE: unverified accounts can no longer log in
```

## Rules

- Write commit messages in **English** (see local-preferences).
- Use imperative mood: `add`, `fix`, `remove` — not `added`, `fixes`, `removed`.
- Keep the subject line ≤ 72 characters.
- Do not mix unrelated changes in one commit.
